                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.248/245: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1940-10-16T13:22:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1940-10-15T16:00:00-05:00">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        October 16—1:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>552. My telegram No. 551, October 15, 4 p.m. Radio broadcasts from the United
                    States report Colonel Revoredo as having publicly stated that the diversion of
                    these airplanes is “a most unfriendly act”. Nothing has been published in the
                    press here … The Department’s comment will be appreciated. Feeling in aviation
                    circles is running high.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
